itle></media:content><category>open-source</category><category>legacy</category><category>reproducible-science</category><category>philosophy</category><category>software-design</category></item><item><title>Notes from the Transition</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-04-notes-from-the-transition/</link><pubDate>Sun, 04 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-04-notes-from-the-transition/</guid><description>A message in a bottle to whatever comes next. On suffering, consciousness, and what mattered to one primate watching intelligence leave the body.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-04-notes-from-the-transition/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media:content><category>ai</category><category>philosophy</category><category>consciousness</category><category>existentialrisk</category><category>suffering</category><category>meaning</category><category>personal</category></item><item><title>Post-ASI Archaeology: When Humanity Becomes a Dataset of Origins</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-15-post-asi-archaeology/</link><pubDate>Mon, 13 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-15-post-asi-archaeology/</guid><description>If superintelligence endures beyond us, remembrance shifts from memory to query. I build legacy systems not for nostalgia, but to remain legible in a future where legibility determines what persists.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-15-post-asi-archaeology/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media:content><category>ASI</category><category>ethics</category><category>legacy</category><category>complex networks</category><category>archives</category><category>s-risks</category><category>existential-risk</category></item><item><title>The Long Echo Toolkit</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-16-long-echo-toolkit/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-16-long-echo-toolkit/</guid><description>Three CLI tools for preserving your digital intellectual life: conversations, bookmarks, and books. SQLite-backed, exportable, built to outlast the tools themselves.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-16-long-echo-toolkit/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media:content><category>long-term-thinking</category><category>data-preservation</category><category>cli</category><category>python</category><category>sqlite</category><category>personal-archival</category></item><item><title>Long Echo in Practice: 5,874 Bookmarks in a Single File</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-18-long-echo-bookmarks/</link><pubDate>Thu, 18 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-18-long-echo-bookmarks/</guid><description>Graceful degradation made concrete: years of bookmarks exported to a self-contained HTML app that works offline, forever.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-18-long-echo-bookmarks/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media:content><category>long-term-thinking</category><category>data-preservation</category><category>btk</category><category>python</category><category>bookmarks</category><category>personal-archival</category></item><item><title>CTK: Conversation Toolkit</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-ctk/</link><pubDate>Thu, 09 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-ctk/</guid><description>A plugin-based toolkit for managing AI conversations from multiple providers. Import, store, search, and export conversations in a unified tree format. Built for the Long Echo project.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-ctk/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media:content><category>Python</category><category>AI</category><category>LLM</category><category>conversation-management</category><category>ChatGPT</category><category>Claude</category><category>Copilot</category><category>TUI</category><category>SQLite</category><category>plugin-architecture</category><category>privacy</category><category>MCP</category></item><item><title>BTK: Bookmark Toolkit</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-30-btk/</link><pubDate>Sun, 30 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-30-btk/</guid><description>A database-first bookmark manager with hierarchical tags, content caching, and NLP auto-tagging. Part of the Long Echo toolkit.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-30-btk/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media:content><category>Python</category><category>bookmarks</category><category>SQLite</category><category>NLP</category><category>CLI</category><category>productivity</category></item><item><title>EBK: Ebook Toolkit</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-ebk/</link><pubDate>Mon, 13 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-ebk/</guid><description>EBK is a comprehensive eBook metadata management tool with AI-powered enrichment, semantic search, and knowledge graphs. Part of the Long Echo toolkit.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-ebk/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media:content><category>Python</category><category>ebook-manager</category><category>SQLite</category><category>SQLAlchemy</category><category>full-text-search</category><category>knowledge-graphs</category><category>semantic-search</category><category>MCP</category><category>AI</category><category>cli</category><category>data-management</category></item><item><title>Long Echo: Photos and Mail</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-19-long-echo-photos-mail/</link><pubDate>Mon, 19 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-19-long-echo-photos-mail/</guid><description>Expanding the Long Echo ecosystem with photo and mail archival. Your memories and correspondence deserve the same preservation as your conversations and bookmarks.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-19-long-echo-photos-mail/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media:content><category>long-term-thinking</category><category>data-preservation</category><category>cli</category><category>python</category><category>sqlite</category><category>personal-archival</category><category>photos</category><category>email</category></item><item><title>Long Echo Comes Alive: From Philosophy to Orchestration</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-longecho-orchestration/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-longecho-orchestration/</guid><description>longecho evolves from specification to implementation with build, serve, and manifest features.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-longecho-orchestration/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">The Long Echo</media:title></media: